# The block devices of USB sticks, drives and card readers belong to the group `users`, which the
# regular account is in, so that it can partition them, make, check and label their file systems,
# the one that gpg-genkey wants among them, and copy them with dd. The SD card is not on USB: it
# stays with root and the group `disk`.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", GROUP="users", MODE="0660"

# A FAT file system of a USB stick that is not labelled KEYS is /dev/usb-storage, which
# mnt-usb\x2dstorage.mount mounts. The KEYS stick has its own mount (mnt-keys.mount, by label), so
# that gpg-genkey never writes a key to another stick. 60-persistent-storage.rules has probed the
# type and the label by now. With two such sticks, the link follows one of them.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ENV{ID_FS_TYPE}=="vfat", ENV{ID_FS_LABEL}!="KEYS", \
    SYMLINK+="usb-storage"
